      "writtenOn": "2021-01-13T19:37:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah - the property itself is also doing something tricky/complicated. I wish we could have \u0027odm_available\u0027 to stay consistent with existing properties, but it sounds extremely hard to implement and formally support everywhere.\n\nWhat happens if we have: libfoo (on /vendor) -\u003e libbar (on /odm) -\u003e libbaz (on /vendor). I think that would resolve in the build system, but will it fail at load time (and if it does, it should be considered a build bug, not to match loading, and if it doesn\u0027t, then it should be considered a bug to have this back and forth dependency chain). Should we explicitly disable this case here?",
      "parentUuid": "5f8d236f_94c233da",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "b9dcda30a922fb37a9bf5f2ba7bccd485fa12a9c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1ffadb4_c288219a",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146974
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-14T00:40:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can try defining odm_available. As all odm_available must be vendor_available, we may update not many places but just the HasVendorVariant() function. (I hope it works.)\n\nlibfoo (on /vendor) -\u003e libbar (on /odm) -\u003e libbaz (on /vendor) is allowed both on runtime and buildtime. That is the same for system -\u003e system_ext -\u003e system. That\u0027s because we don\u0027t have separate namespaces for each partition.\nAs these partitions are tightly coupled, I don\u0027t think it must be blocked.",
      "parentUuid": "7ebfb4e6_8d782d9e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "b9dcda30a922fb37a9bf5f2ba7bccd485fa12a9c",
